    ('provincial-smelt-bay-park', 'Smelt Bay Park', 'provincial', 50.031574, -124.993326, 'Discovery Islands', 'At the south end of Cortes Island, Smelt Bay is named for capelin that spawn along the shore in early autumn. Its beach is suited to low-tide marine exploration, with camping and views along the bay toward Sutil Point.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1098', NULL),
