    ('provincial-spectacle-lake-park', 'Spectacle Lake Park', 'provincial', 48.578882, -123.570243, 'South Island', 'Mature forest, wetlands and a spring-fed lake create a compact nature area northwest of Victoria. Visitors can swim, fish, walk a trail that circles the lake, and in winter sometimes skate when conditions allow.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1110', NULL),
    ('provincial-spider-lake-park', 'Spider Lake Park', 'provincial', 49.34349, -124.633304, 'Central Island', 'Warm water and a small sandy beach make Spider Lake a popular place for swimming and picnics. Canoeists and kayakers can follow the shoreline into quieter bays west of Qualicum Beach.', 'https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/parks-ecological-reserves-and-protected-areas', 'BC Parks / DataBC — TANTALIS protected areas', '1111', NULL),
