    ('regional-roche-cove-regional-park', 'Roche Cove Regional Park', 'regional', 48.372623, -123.620204, 'Capital Region', 'Trails wind through temperate rainforest beside a cool creek and sheltered cove. The calm water is also suited to paddling, especially in the quiet morning.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-sandy-pool-regional-park', 'Sandy Pool Regional Park', 'regional', 48.758545, -123.834765, 'Cowichan Valley', 'A sandy beach and swimming holes on the Cowichan River draw summer visitors, while forest paths extend for more than a kilometre and include interpretive signs. The park also has a drift-boat launch and seasonal toilets.', 'https://maps.cvrd.ca/mapservices/rest/services/Parks/MapServer/2', 'Cowichan Valley Regional District — Parks GIS layer', '980395', NULL),
    ('regional-sea-to-sea-regional-park', 'Sea to Sea Regional Park', 'regional', 48.456765, -123.689212, 'Capital Region', 'This nearly 4,000-hectare wilderness area forms part of a protected corridor from Saanich Inlet to Juan de Fuca Strait. High points such as Mount Manuel Quimper and Mount Brule offer expansive views across the Sooke Hills.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-sooke-hills-wilderness-regional-park', 'Sooke Hills Wilderness Regional Park', 'regional', 48.448245, -123.60612, 'Capital Region', 'This large wilderness area borders the Greater Victoria Water Supply Area and includes Mount Braden, one of the highest peaks in the Capital Regional District park system at 471 metres.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-sooke-potholes-regional-park', 'Sooke Potholes Regional Park', 'regional', 48.447059, -123.727756, 'Capital Region', 'Glacially carved pools and smooth rock formations line the Sooke River, where salmon return each fall. Fast-moving water shaped the potholes in the sandstone valley, making the river’s geology the park’s central feature.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-sooke-river-regional-park', 'Sooke River Park', 'regional', 48.389814, -123.702495, 'Capital Region', 'No visitor overview is available in the CRD parks map layer; it identifies the mapped park name and feature.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-st-john-point-regional-park', 'St. John Point Regional Park', 'regional', 48.817716, -123.236838, 'Gulf Islands', 'This North Pender waterfront park has two beaches, an informal perimeter route and a more rugged path along rocky bluffs. It is a quiet place for a coastal walk and birdwatching.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-stoney-hill-regional-park', 'Stoney Hill Regional Park', 'regional', 48.782682, -123.568625, 'Cowichan Valley', 'A 3.2-kilometre loop climbs through the forest above Sansum Narrows, with views toward Salt Spring Island and the surrounding coast. The trail begins and ends at the parking area, which holds about 25 vehicles.', 'https://maps.cvrd.ca/mapservices/rest/services/Parks/MapServer/2', 'Cowichan Valley Regional District — Parks GIS layer', '980399', NULL),
    ('regional-thetis-lake-regional-park', 'Thetis Lake Regional Park', 'regional', 48.481234, -123.477401, 'Capital Region', 'Thetis Lake is a popular swimming and walking destination with more than 40 kilometres of recreation trails. Designated as Canada’s first nature sanctuary in 1958, the park combines protected natural areas with a broad trail network.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-witty-s-lagoon-regional-park', 'Witty''s Lagoon Regional Park', 'regional', 48.385708, -123.517546, 'Capital Region', 'Woodland trails lead through a varied seashore landscape of creek, salt marsh, sandy beach and rocky headlands. The mix of habitats supports abundant birdlife and other wildlife.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL),
    ('regional-wrigglesworth-lake-regional-park', 'Wrigglesworth Lake Regional Park', 'regional', 48.520434, -123.573165, 'Capital Region', 'A trail from Goldstream Heights Drive leads to the lake in this small park beside Sooke Hills Wilderness Regional Park. The lake is the focal point of the visit.', 'https://mapservices.crd.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/Basemap/Basemap/MapServer/3', 'Capital Regional District — Park GIS layer', NULL, NULL)
